  - id: C:event/founding
    type: event
    name: Foundation founded in Florida
    summary: The Wikimedia Foundation is founded on 2003-06-20.
    at: 2003-06-20
    visibility: public
    provenance: {mode: net-scan, sources: ["https://foundation.wikimedia.org/wiki/Memory:Timeline"], confidence: 0.9, state: known}

  - id: C:event/headquarters-move
    type: event
    name: Headquarters moves to San Francisco
    summary: The move from Florida to San Francisco, announced 2007-10-09, is complete on 2008-01-31.
    at: 2008-01-31
    visibility: public
    provenance: {mode: net-scan, sources: ["https://foundation.wikimedia.org/wiki/Memory:Timeline"], confidence: 0.9, state: known}

  - id: C:event/board-expansion
    type: event
    name: Board of Trustees expanded to up to 16
    summary: The Board is expanded in 2020 to up to 16 Trustees, the size the bylaws now allow.
    year: 2020
    visibility: public
    provenance: {mode: net-scan, sources: ["https://foundation.wikimedia.org/wiki/Memory:Timeline", "https://meta.wikimedia.org/wiki/Wikimedia_Foundation/Board_of_Trustees"], confidence: 0.85, state: known}

  - id: C:event/enterprise-launch
    type: event
    name: Wikimedia Enterprise launches
    summary: Announced 2021-03-16 and launched publicly on 2021-10-25, as a commercial service for large reusers of Wikimedia content.
    at: 2021-10-25
    visibility: public
    provenance: {mode: net-scan, sources: ["https://foundation.wikimedia.org/wiki/Wikimedia_Enterprise", "https://foundation.wikimedia.org/wiki/Memory:Timeline"], confidence: 0.9, state: known}

  - id: C:event/first-enterprise-customers
    type: event
    name: First Enterprise customers announced
    summary: Google and the Internet Archive are named as the first Wikimedia Enterprise customers, and free trials open to self sign-up.
    at: 2022-06-21
    visibility: public
    provenance: {mode: net-scan, sources: ["https://wikimediafoundation.org/news/2022/06/21/wikimedia-enterprise-announces-google-and-internet-archive-first-customers/"], confidence: 0.8, state: known}

  - id: C:event/endowment-standalone
    type: event
    name: Endowment becomes a standalone organization
    summary: On 2023-09-30 the Wikimedia Endowment starts as a separate 501(c)(3) with its own Board; the net assets Tides Foundation had held for it ($116.2M) move to it.
    at: 2023-09-30
    visibility: public
    provenance: {mode: net-scan, sources: ["https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/foundation/3/3f/Wikimedia_Foundation_FY_24-25_Audit_Report.pdf", "https://wikimediaendowment.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Wikimedia-Endowment-Audit-Report-FY-24-25.pdf", "https://meta.wikimedia.org/wiki/Wikimedia_Endowment_reports/Financial/Form_990/2024-2025_-_frequently_asked_questions"], confidence: 0.9, state: known}

  - id: C:event/enterprise-partners-named
    type: event
    name: Enterprise partners named on Wikipedia's 25th birthday
    summary: On 2026-01-15 the Foundation and Wikimedia Enterprise name Amazon, Meta, Microsoft, Mistral AI and Perplexity among the partners, beside Google and others; financial terms are not disclosed.
    at: 2026-01-15
    visibility: public
    provenance: {mode: net-scan, sources: ["https://enterprise.wikimedia.com/blog/wikipedia-25-enterprise-partners/", "https://wikimediafoundation.org/news/2026/01/15/wikipedia-celebrates-25years/"], confidence: 0.85, state: known}

  - id: C:asset/headquarters-lease
    type: asset
    name: Headquarters lease, San Francisco
    summary: The office at 1 Sansome Street; a non-cancelable remaining term of 3.25 years at 30 June 2025 with one option of five more; the lease at 1 Montgomery Street was not renewed in 2024.
